<title>SLOVAKIA: BIATHLON-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP MEN'S 7.5 KM RELAY RESULTS.</title>
<headline>BIATHLON-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP MEN'S 7.5 KM RELAY RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>OSRBLIE, Slovakia 1997-02-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading results of the</p>
<p>men's 7.5-km relay event at the World Biathlon Championship on</p>
<p>Sunday:</p>
<p>1. Germany (Ricco Gross, Peter Sendel, Sven Fischer, Frank</p>
<p>    Luck)	1 hour 17 minutes 42.5 minutes, no penalty lap</p>
<p>2. Norway (Egil Gjelland, Jon Age Tyldum, Dag Bjoerndalen, Ole</p>
<p>    Einar Bjoerndalen)			  1:17:48.2/0</p>
<p>3. Italy (Rene Cattarinussi, Wilfried Pallhuber, Patrick</p>
<p>    Favre, Pier Alberto Carrara)	    1:19:10.4/1</p>
<p>4. Belarus (Alexei Aidarov, Vadim Sashurin, Alexander Popov,</p>
<p>    Oleg Ryzhenkov)			     1:19:25.9/1</p>
<p>5. France (Julien Robert, Patrice Bailly-Salins, Thierry</p>
<p>    Dusserre, Raphael Poiree)		 1:19:38.7/0</p>
<p>6. Poland (Wieslaw Ziemianin, Tomasz, Sikora, Jan Ziemianin,</p>
<p>    Wojciach Kozub)			     1:19:56.8/0</p>
<p>7. Finland ( Ville Raikkonen, Vesa Pontio, Harri Eloranta,</p>
<p>    Vesa Hietalahti)			    1:20:09.2/0</p>
<p>8. Russia (Viktor Maigurov, Vladimir Dratchev, Sergei Tarasov,</p>
<p>    Pavel Rostovtsev)			   1:20:09.6/1</p>
<p>9. Estonia (Janno Prants, Indrek Tobreluts, Kalju Ojaste,</p>
<p>    Dimitri Borovik)			    1:21:12.4/0</p>
<p>10.Austria (Wolfgang Perner, Ludwig Gredler, Wolfgang</p>
<p>    Rottmann, Reinhard Neuner)		1:21:32.1/2</p>
</text>
